# Roblox Studio

### Core Scripting Instances
* **Script (Server Script):** Executes code on the server to handle game logic, data saving, and authority over all players.
* **LocalScript:** Executes code on individual client devices to handle player inputs, camera movement, and client-only UI updates.
* **ModuleScript:** Stores reusable Luau code that can be called and shared across multiple Scripts and LocalScripts.

---

### User Interface (UI) Elements
* **ScreenGui:** A container object placed in StarterGui that renders 2D user interfaces onto the player's screen.
* **Frame:** A rectangular container used to group, align, and organize other UI elements together.
* **TextLabel:** Displays non-interactive static text to the player on the screen or in world space.
* **TextButton:** A clickable button that fires events when pressed by a player to trigger UI actions or scripts.
* **TextBox:** An interactive input field allowing players to type custom text entries into the UI.
* **ImageLabel / ImageButton:** Visual UI elements that render custom textures, icons, or clickable graphic buttons.

---

### Core Services
* **Workspace:** The 3D physical world container that holds all visible parts, models, terrains, and physical objects.
* **ReplicatedStorage:** A shared container where assets, modules, and events are accessible by both server and client.
* **ServerScriptService:** A secure server-only container used to hold and run main game server scripts.
* **ServerStorage:** A secure server-only storage area for assets, maps, and templates hidden from the client.
* **StarterGui:** Holds UI templates that automatically clone into a player's PlayerGui upon spawning.
* **StarterPlayer:** Contains default movement settings and character/player scripts loaded when a player joins.
* **Lighting:** Controls global environmental light, atmospheric effects, shadows, and time-of-day visuals.
* **SoundService:** Manages global game audio properties, sound groups, and audio listener effects.

---

### Physics & Communication
* **Part:** The fundamental 3D building block used to construct physical structures and geometry in the world.
* **Model:** A grouped collection of parts and instances treated as a single unified object.
* **RemoteEvent:** Enables one-way asynchronous communication between the server and client scripts.
* **RemoteFunction:** Enables two-way synchronous requests with a returned response between server and client.
* **BindableEvent:** Allows one-way signal communication strictly between scripts on the same side (server-to-server or client-to-client).
